<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cooperative Cyber Defence Centre of Excellence</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">2008–</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a> · Also known as CCDCOE</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> Cooperative Cyber Defence Centre of Excellence is a research and training centre on cyber defence in Tallinn, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>. Proposed by Estonia and established in 2008, the year after large cyberattacks on Estonian government and banking websites, it supports NATO members with research, exercises and legal analysis, and produced the Tallinn Manual on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/international-law">international law</a> in cyber warfare.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cooperative-cyber-defence-centre-of-excellence.jpg" alt="Cooperative Cyber Defence Centre of Excellence" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Worldlydev · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_NATO_Cooperative_Cyber_Defence_Centre_of_Excellence.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
